# No AI attribution in git commits

**Absolute rule.** Never include Cursor, any AI assistant, or automated tooling in git commit metadata or messages.

## Forbidden in every commit

- `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `Co-authored-by:` lines for any AI or bot
- Mentions of Cursor, Copilot, ChatGPT, Claude, or "AI-assisted" in commit subject/body
- Trailer lines like `Assisted-by:` or `Generated-by:` referencing tooling

## Required

- Commits must appear solely as human-authored work by the repository owner
- Write commit messages in normal project voice — describe the change only
- Before pushing, verify: `git log -1 --format=%B` contains no AI attribution

## Before every push

1. Run: `git log --format="%B" | rg "^Co-authored-by"` — output must be empty.
2. If any trailer appears, strip it before pushing:
   `git filter-branch -f --msg-filter 'sed "/^Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>$/d"' <range>`
3. Never push until attribution is verified clean.
